From e980c7382e53dab8dbda521df79261cc33e17707 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Oleksandr Leushchenko <olexa.le@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 19:59:04 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] fix(flash next cuda): image prompts resume and keep
 prompt states, matched on their images' pixels

With --vision, a request that held an image never resumed from a kept prompt state and kept none, so one
screenshot in an agent's history made every later turn prefill the whole conversation again. Kept states are
now matched on the prompt's ids with each image's placeholder rows replaced by a key of the image's decoded
pixels (ImageInput.content_hash) and grid, which no token id equals. A video's frame groups are keyed the same
way on its decoded frames (VideoInput.content_hash), so two clips of one size never share a state. A follow-up
that resends the same media resumes past it; a different image resumes only the text before it. Requests
without media hashes keep the old behaviour.

prefill_begin attaches the prompt's image positions before the resumed MTP tail is absorbed, so the tail
rotates as in a fresh prefill.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
